 "description": "SEST PC TEST, not a campaign to play. Fog of war is off. January, the southern summer. A Chilean frigate in the Bransfield Strait, a British frigate in the western Weddell pack (65.4S 45W, about 51 % ice), HMS Astute under it 48 nm south (66.2S 45W, about 69 %) and an ice-free control in the Drake Passage, with Russian frigates closing on the first two from open water. Group S5 off Elephant Island must cross the ice edge to reach a Russian picket in the pack (67.75S 58W); with SEST's sea ice on, the campaign map shows the ice edge and slows S5 in the ice.",
